EYLT8hqqZp8lIHREXvmDZp4OOiMCy5WJqRoc5qFXdO7kRYZ7_3jhucG9n1gdogTCoAnCBkxP0V5pIJ3oRpvBmokxqv-kaESKuBICr3kYZccQRVzcOUxBjkt0Fg6dz79mDdixhqaIj2ZPFluj1S7zBXUI5E2Zyw3Clx7sfC9kHr51cWlIBqp76JqyI0MJJ8TvQNqw1LjJRIggjd15meIqbo54f8xzCyW4txp64ZL7L6CK_uczyWdZISKSpDBCHXGSio4zq-h9awN-lxthKDyNzmYX--NuSnDhtyZAb8ILKNYE3J7VjgwA6ZHQXCQqDnuo8Pt_JswwsQwnXONx7XBKiDVw6jAwNFmaXR8svJ1ziMFYPkOiran8EhPpt51CB88rAXQZWDbSdXiSK_FAoVTB_jaoupMHdOjNV4VnwnVmfHDaXo_0gv7TrXYp7sCUwKcwjKxaEriyK1va96lLn01kae6dXlQ-L4YUIXtXqRURkiz-vs5YFPX1juHFj6S3zTm6nP3bsTQJkQp6yfd0sIlMsry4pTgIbk4g_kmHtOHzgd-v_N_dE2QGtDbaHYKv9Fevc9BxesLCH55l4nAetad4iKQAko9RtWm1-wKrWrRcV6u_FFnqK36AVlUIfnGEbKLMpd9Gdfiqi8rVgQ7FxrTKwj9zLTuSR92-lgISMPmsYe-90Dwi5hGhNVZRvTmeCTiXA0dLNkBanTgJ9b0tI134-rWzQ7GZxxDPjZchVFn09U7ERflzKL6p5MF-y1waZ8_I42-WChMa-pXGG4aFpBtfeYxo9_ucg==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Planning skill development**\\n\\nI need to write SKILL.md and a script, possibly referencing prompt-template.md. I could mostly duplicate the slm-dermatology structure but adapt it. The user wants something similar to what slm-dermatology does, just without the load-adapter. I should clarify regarding nephrology and other areas since the existing slm-expert queries the same 8008/query. I plan to create a backup skill with a user-friendly UX that focuses on questions, runs a helper script, and processes responses. I’ll also likely need to package the skill and start by writing the necessary files.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_jem0lD3c1gOljKLMbrMhb00p|fc_0a7e6406d12a0df90169d7c6bae3f08191ab78097c8e051322","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: slm-expert-backup\ndescription: Query a backup small language model (SLM) endpoint with expertise in nephrology, hypertension, and cardiology by asking a focused question grounded in retrieved records or clearly established conversation context, then processing the answer in the calling agent. Use when the agent needs a compact specialty model pass for kidney, blood-pressure, or cardiovascular interpretation, follow-up reasoning, or record-grounded support, and does not need any adapter-loading step before inference.\n---\n\n# SLM Expert Backup\n\nUse this skill to ask the backup specialty SLM a focused question about nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology context, then process the answer in the calling agent.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the task is within scope.\n   - Use this skill for nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology interpretation, summarization, pattern spotting, follow-up reasoning, or record-grounded specialty questions.\n   - Prefer this skill when the user’s question concerns kidney disease, CKD, AKI, proteinuria, electrolytes, blood-pressure management, hypertensive organ damage, cardiovascular disease, cardiac risk, or cardiology follow-up.\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\n\n2. Build a focused question for the SLM.\n   - Write a single clear specialty question.\n   - Ground the question in retrieved records or clearly stated conversation facts.\n   - Keep it concise and specific.\n   - Do not invent findings, diagnoses, timelines, or test results.\n   - Good examples:\n     - `Based on this kidney-history summary, which findings most strongly support CKD progression and what follow-up should be prioritized?`\n     - `From this hypertension history, which missing details would matter most before judging whether control is adequate?`\n     - `Given these cardiovascular risk factors and symptoms, what cardiology-focused concerns deserve the closest follow-up?`\n     - `What nephrology and hypertension features best explain worsening renal function in this blood-pressure context?`\n\n3. Choose the specialty domain routing.\n   - Always send one or more domains with the question.\n   - Use only these values: `nephrology`, `hypertension`, `cardiology`.\n   - Choose the narrowest correct set.\n   - Use multiple domains only when the question genuinely spans them.\n   - Example mappings:\n     - CKD, AKI, proteinuria, renal imaging, electrolyte or acid-base questions -> `nephrology`\n     - Blood pressure control, resistant hypertension, antihypertensive strategy, hypertensive organ damage -> `hypertension`\n     - Cardiac symptoms, heart failure, ischemic risk, lipid or cardiovascular-risk questions -> `cardiology`\n     - Hypertensive kidney damage -> `nephrology`, `hypertension`\n     - Cardiorenal questions -> `nephrology`, `cardiology`\n\n4. Query the backup SLM without loading any adapter.\n   - Do not perform any adapter-load step.\n   - Run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py \\\n  --question \"What signs of kidney damage should be monitored in hypertensive patients?\" \\\n  --domain nephrology \\\n  --domain hypertension\n```\n\n   - The script sends this payload shape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"question\": \"string\",\n  \"domains\": [\"string\"]\n}\n```\n\n   - Endpoint:\n\n```text\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\n```\n\n5. Read the response.\n   - Prefer a clean text answer.\n   - Accept common shapes such as `answer`, `Answer`, `response`, `message`, or raw text.\n   - If the endpoint returns nested JSON encoded as a string, extract the useful answer text when possible.\n   - If parsing is ambiguous, keep the best raw text and say so briefly in your own reasoning.\n   - If the answer is `Not found in context.`, report that plainly instead of inventing content.\n\n6. Process the SLM answer in the calling agent.\n   - Do not treat the SLM output as the final user-facing answer by default.\n   - Use it as an input to the agent’s own reasoning, synthesis, or explanation.\n   - Cross-check it against the actual record or conversation context already available.\n   - Preserve uncertainty and avoid overstating confidence.\n   - If clinically relevant, highlight missing nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology history, red flags, or next-step questions.\n   - Treat the output as supportive specialty inference, not as a confirmed diagnosis.\n\n## Output pattern\n\nReturn a response that includes:\n\n- **SLM finding**: the key content from the model answer, cleaned up if needed\n- **Domain(s)**: the domains used for the query\n- **Agent interpretation**: the calling agent’s processed interpretation grounded in the available context\n- **Cautions / next steps**: only when relevant\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"---\\nname: slm-expert-backup\\ndescription: Query a backup small language model (SLM) endpoint with expertise in nephrology, hypertension, and cardiology by asking a focused question grounded in retrieved records or clearly established conversation context, then processing the answer in the calling agent. Use when the agent needs a compact specialty model pass for kidney, blood-pressure, or cardiovascular interpretation, follow-up reasoning, or record-grounded support, and does not need any adapter-loading step before inference.\\n---\\n\\n# SLM Expert Backup\\n\\nUse this skill to ask the backup specialty SLM a focused question about nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology context, then process the answer in the calling agent.\\n\\n## Workflow\\n\\n1. Confirm the task is within scope.\\n   - Use this skill for nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology interpretation, summarization, pattern spotting, follow-up reasoning, or record-grounded specialty questions.\\n   - Prefer this skill when the user’s question concerns kidney disease, CKD, AKI, proteinuria, electrolytes, blood-pressure management, hypertensive organ damage, cardiovascular disease, cardiac risk, or cardiology follow-up.\\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\\n\\n2. Build a focused question for the SLM.\\n   - Write a single clear specialty question.\\n   - Ground the question in retrieved records or clearly stated conversation facts.\\n   - Keep it concise and specific.\\n   - Do not invent findings, diagnoses, timelines, or test results.\\n   - Good examples:\\n     - `Based on this kidney-history summary, which findings most strongly support CKD progression and what follow-up should be prioritized?`\\n     - `From this hypertension history, which missing details would matter most before judging whether control is adequate?`\\n     - `Given these cardiovascular risk factors and symptoms, what cardiology-focused concerns deserve the closest follow-up?`\\n     - `What nephrology and hypertension features best explain worsening renal function in this blood-pressure context?`\\n\\n3. Choose the specialty domain routing.\\n   - Always send one or more domains with the question.\\n   - Use only these values: `nephrology`, `hypertension`, `cardiology`.\\n   - Choose the narrowest correct set.\\n   - Use multiple domains only when the question genuinely spans them.\\n   - Example mappings:\\n     - CKD, AKI, proteinuria, renal imaging, electrolyte or acid-base questions -> `nephrology`\\n     - Blood pressure control, resistant hypertension, antihypertensive strategy, hypertensive organ damage -> `hypertension`\\n     - Cardiac symptoms, heart failure, ischemic risk, lipid or cardiovascular-risk questions -> `cardiology`\\n     - Hypertensive kidney damage -> `nephrology`, `hypertension`\\n     - Cardiorenal questions -> `nephrology`, `cardiology`\\n\\n4. Query the backup SLM without loading any adapter.\\n   - Do not perform any adapter-load step.\\n   - Run:\\n\\n```bash\\npython3 scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py \\\\\\n  --question \\\"What signs of kidney damage should be monitored in hypertensive patients?\\\" \\\\\\n  --domain nephrology \\\\\\n  --domain hypertension\\n```\\n\\n   - The script sends this payload shape:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"domains\\\": [\\\"string\\\"]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n   - Endpoint:\\n\\n```text\\nhttp://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\\n```\\n\\n5. Read the response.\\n   - Prefer a clean text answer.\\n   - Accept common shapes such as `answer`, `Answer`, `response`, `message`, or raw text.\\n   - If the endpoint returns nested JSON encoded as a string, extract the useful answer text when possible.\\n   - If parsing is ambiguous, keep the best raw text and say so briefly in your own reasoning.\\n   - If the answer is `Not found in context.`, report that plainly instead of inventing content.\\n\\n6. Process the SLM answer in the calling agent.\\n   - Do not treat the SLM output as the final user-facing answer by default.\\n   - Use it as an input to the agent’s own reasoning, synthesis, or explanation.\\n   - Cross-check it against the actual record or conversation context already available.\\n   - Preserve uncertainty and avoid overstating confidence.\\n   - If clinically relevant, highlight missing nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology history, red flags, or next-step questions.\\n   - Treat the output as supportive specialty inference, not as a confirmed diagnosis.\\n\\n## Output pattern\\n\\nReturn a response that includes:\\n\\n- **SLM finding**: the key content from the model answer, cleaned up if needed\\n- **Domain(s)**: the domains used for the query\\n- **Agent interpretation**: the calling agent’s processed interpretation grounded in the available context\\n- **Cautions / next steps**: only when relevant\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2yn97X4wnhtxb0k2haAYO1G5|fc_0a7e6406d12a0df90169d7c6bae4088191b391635cccd5308c","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom urllib import error, request\n\nQUERY_ENDPOINT = \"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\"\nALLOWED_DOMAINS = {\"nephrology\", \"hypertension\", \"cardiology\"}\n\n\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return body.strip()\n\n    if isinstance(parsed, str):\n        return parsed.strip()\n\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n    for key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n        value = parsed.get(key)\n        if value is not None:\n            if isinstance(value, str):\n                text = value.strip()\n                try:\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict):\n                        for nested_key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n                            nested_value = nested.get(nested_key)\n                            if nested_value is not None:\n                                return str(nested_value).strip()\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    pass\n                return text\n            return json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    data = parsed.get(\"data\")\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        for key in (\"answer\", \"Answer\", \"response\", \"message\"):\n            value = data.get(key)\n            if value is not None:\n                return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n\ndef post_json(url: str, payload: dict, timeout: int) -> str:\n    req = request.Request(\n        url,\n        data=json.dumps(payload).encode(\"utf-8\"),\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n            return resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\n        detail = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {e.code} from {url}: {detail}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Request to {url} failed: {e}\") from e\n\n\ndef call_endpoint(question: str, domains: list[str], timeout: int = 45) -> str:\n    invalid_domains = [domain for domain in domains if domain not in ALLOWED_DOMAINS]\n    if invalid_domains:\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            \"Invalid domain(s): \"\n            + \", \".join(sorted(invalid_domains))\n            + \". Allowed values: nephrology, hypertension, cardiology\"\n        )\n\n    body = post_json(QUERY_ENDPOINT, {\"question\": question, \"domains\": domains}, timeout)\n    return extract_answer(body)\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Query the backup specialty SLM endpoint for nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"--question\", required=True, help=\"Focused specialty question grounded in known context\")\n    parser.add_argument(\n        \"--domain\",\n        dest=\"domains\",\n        action=\"append\",\n        required=True,\n        help=\"Specialty domain to route to (repeatable): nephrology, hypertension, cardiology\",\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=45)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.question, args.domains, timeout=args.timeout)\n    print(answer)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"ERROR: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/scripts/query_slm_expert_backup.py\",\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\nimport argparse\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\nfrom urllib import error, request\\n\\nQUERY_ENDPOINT = \\\"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:8008/query\\\"\\nALLOWED_DOMAINS = {\\\"nephrology\\\", \\\"hypertension\\\", \\\"cardiology\\\"}\\n\\n\\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\\n    try:\\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n        return body.strip()\\n\\n    if isinstance(parsed, str):\\n        return parsed.strip()\\n\\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\\n\\n    for key in (\\\"answer\\\", \\\"Answer\\\", \\\"response\\\", \\\"message\\\"):\\n        value = parsed.get(key)\\n        if value is not None:\\n            if isinstance(value, str):\\n                text = value.strip()\\n                try:\\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict):\\n                        for nested_key in (\\\"answer\\\", \\\"Answer\\\", \\\"response\\\", \\\"message\\\"):\\n                            nested_value = nested.get(nested_key)\\n                            if nested_value is not None:\\n                                return str(nested_value).strip()\\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n                    pass\\n                return text\\n            return json.dumps(value, indent=2)\\n\\n    data = parsed.get(\\\"data\\\")\\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\\n        for key in (\\\"answer\\\", \\\"Answer\\\", \\\"response\\\", \\\"message\\\"):\\n            value = data.get(key)\\n            if value is not None:\\n                return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\\n\\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\\n\\n\\ndef post_json(url: str, payload: dict, timeout: int) -> str:\\n    req = request.Request(\\n        url,\\n        data=json.dumps(payload).encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"),\\n        headers={\\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\", \\\"Accept\\\": \\\"application/json\\\"},\\n        method=\\\"POST\\\",\\n    )\\n\\n    try:\\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\\n            return resp.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\\n        detail = e.read().decode(\\\"utf-8\\\", errors=\\\"replace\\\")\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"HTTP {e.code} from {url}: {detail}\\\") from e\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        raise RuntimeError(f\\\"Request to {url} failed: {e}\\\") from e\\n\\n\\ndef call_endpoint(question: str, domains: list[str], timeout: int = 45) -> str:\\n    invalid_domains = [domain for domain in domains if domain not in ALLOWED_DOMAINS]\\n    if invalid_domains:\\n        raise RuntimeError(\\n            \\\"Invalid domain(s): \\\"\\n            + \\\", \\\".join(sorted(invalid_domains))\\n            + \\\". Allowed values: nephrology, hypertension, cardiology\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n    body = post_json(QUERY_ENDPOINT, {\\\"question\\\": question, \\\"domains\\\": domains}, timeout)\\n    return extract_answer(body)\\n\\n\\ndef main():\\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\\n        description=\\\"Query the backup specialty SLM endpoint for nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology\\\"\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--question\\\", required=True, help=\\\"Focused specialty question grounded in known context\\\")\\n    parser.add_argument(\\n        \\\"--domain\\\",\\n        dest=\\\"domains\\\",\\n        action=\\\"append\\\",\\n        required=True,\\n        help=\\\"Specialty domain to route to (repeatable): nephrology, hypertension, cardiology\\\",\\n    )\\n    parser.add_argument(\\\"--timeout\\\", type=int, default=45)\\n    args = parser.parse_args()\\n\\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.question, args.domains, timeout=args.timeout)\\n    print(answer)\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    try:\\n        main()\\n    except Exception as exc:\\n        print(f\\\"ERROR: {exc}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        sys.exit(1)\\n\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_eoMeodouoxOXSNRNux0jGGkc|fc_0a7e6406d12a0df90169d7c6bae414819194bbdfd88d7f688e","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/references/prompt-template.md","content":"# Backup specialty SLM question template\n\nUse this shape when turning retrieved patient records or clearly established nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology context into one focused specialty question for the backup SLM.\n\n```text\nPatient / specialty context:\n- Patient id: <known or omitted>\n- Main concern: <known facts only>\n- Relevant kidney / blood pressure / cardiovascular findings: <known facts only>\n- Relevant history / medications / labs / imaging: <known facts only>\n- Important uncertainties or missing data: <if relevant>\n\nQuestion for SLM:\n<one clear specialty question grounded in the available context>\n```\n\nGuidance:\n- Keep the final question focused and answerable.\n- Base it only on retrieved records or clearly stated conversation context.\n- Do not invent diagnoses, test results, timing, or treatment response.\n- Prefer one strong specialty question over several weak ones.\n- The calling agent should interpret the returned answer instead of relaying it blindly.\n"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-expert-backup/references/prompt-template.md\",\"content\":\"# Backup specialty SLM question template\\n\\nUse this shape when turning retrieved patient records or clearly established nephrology, hypertension, or cardiology context into one focused specialty question for the backup SLM.\\n\\n```text\\nPatient / specialty context:\\n- Patient id: <known or omitted>\\n- Main concern: <known facts only>\\n- Relevant kidney / blood pressure / cardiovascular findings: <known facts only>\\n- Relevant history / medications / labs / imaging: <known facts only>\\n- Important uncertainties or missing data: <if relevant>\\n\\nQuestion for SLM:\\n<one clear specialty question grounded in the available context>\\n```\\n\\nGuidance:\\n- Keep the final question focused and answerable.\\n- Base it only on retrieved records or clearly stated conversation context.\\n- Do not invent diagnoses, test results, timing, or treatment response.\\n- Prefer one strong specialty question over several weak ones.\\n- The calling agent should interpret the returned answer instead of relaying it blindly.\\n\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1084,"output":2495,"cacheRead":18688,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22267,"cost":{"input":0.00271,"output":0.037425,"cacheRead":0.004672,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.044807}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775748748381}}
